::U3L2-01::A food Calorie generally means a {=kilocalorie ~gram ~vitamin ~serving}

::U3L2-02::Energy intake is {=energy obtained from foods and beverages ~only exercise energy ~a weight target ~activity intensity}

::U3L2-03::Energy expenditure includes {=basic functions, activity, and other physiological processes ~activity only ~food only ~body weight only}

::U3L2-04::Basal energy needs support {=essential body functions at rest ~vigorous activity only ~protein digestion only ~body-size measurement}

::U3L2-05::Metabolism refers to {=chemical processes that sustain life and use energy ~exercise duration ~one universal energy value ~body appearance}

::U3L2-06::Energy balance describes {=the relationship between intake and expenditure over time ~a command to minimize intake ~activity only ~appearance}

::U3L2-07::An estimated value is {=an informed approximation ~always exact ~a diagnosis ~a prescription}

::U3L2-08::Which variable may influence an activity estimate? {=Intensity ~Page color ~Question number ~Course title}

